    <bpmn:process id="W_W5569" name="W5569. Mass-Commute Disruption &amp; Transport-Strike Continuity Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A citywide or regional commute interruption threatening mass absenteeism on a trading day — a PUV/jeepney strike or transport-group protest, major-flood or landslide road closures on primary commute corridors, or a fuel-supply disruption idling commuter transport across a metro where BuildRight concentrates stores and a DC
Frequency: ~2–5 disruption events per year across the operating regions (transport-group strikes recur with modernization policy cycles; flood-season road closures are annual); most resolve within one day, the rare multi-day event is the tail case
Volume: 1 event × the affected metro&#x27;s sites (30–80 stores + 1 DC) × the affected sites&#x27; crews (typically 30–60% of store headcount commutes by public transport) × the trading day&#x27;s staffing requirement
Owner: Transport Lead / Fleet Planning (VS-06) (continuity protocol); Site Managers (attendance execution)
Participants: Store/DC Managers (site staffing decisions), HR Shared Services (VS-103.1 attendance &amp; leave placement), Regional Managers (multi-site calls), Fleet Dispatch (shuttle surge per W4250), Payroll (VS-19.2, attendance coding), VS-19.3 (scheduling), Communications/VS-63 (employee &amp; customer messaging), Regional Manager closure authority (the E-02 custody where trading cannot be sustained)
Source: workflow W5569 — Mass-Commute Disruption &amp; Transport-Strike Continuity Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5569_LaneSet7">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5569_Lane1" name="Transport Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5569_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5569_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5569_Start8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5569_Lane2" name="HR Shared Services">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5569_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5569_Lane3" name="Fleet Dispatch">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5569_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5569_Lane4" name="Regional Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5569_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5569_Lane5" name="VS-63">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5569_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5569_Lane6" name="Payroll">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5569_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5569_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5569_Start8" name="A citywide or regional commute interruption threatening mass absenteeism on a trading day…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5569_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5569_Task9" name="Disruptor &amp; scope call">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Disruptor &amp; scope call: classify the event (strike vs flood-closure vs fuel) from news/authoritative feeds; map affected corridors against the site roster; forecast attendance impact per site from commute-mode data (W4251/W4253 profiles)
Responsible (R): Transport Lead
Accountable (A): HR Shared Services
Duration: 1–2 hours (day before or 5–6 AM)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5569_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5569_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5569_Task10" name="Attendance directive">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Attendance directive: site-level staffing directive — report-if-you-can with no-penalty absence coding for stranded crews; critical-role matrix activates (keyholders, cashiers, receiving; department minimums)
Responsible (R): HR Shared Services / Site Managers
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: Same morning</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5569_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5569_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5569_Task11" name="Continuity transport">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Continuity transport: shuttle surge on consolidated pickup points (W4250 manifest discipline), ride-share/van-pool allowance activation per W4253 for critical roles, carpool coordination via the site channels
Responsible (R): Fleet Dispatch / Transport Lead
Accountable (A): Transport Lead
Duration: Event-long</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5569_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5569_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5569_Task12" name="Trading decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Trading decision: open-with-skeleton-crew is the default with service-level expectations set (lane count, services suspended); where staffing or safety cannot sustain trading, closure rides the E-02 custody — W2510&#x27;s decision matrix, W850&#x27;s mechanics; documented either way
Responsible (R): Regional Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: On threshold</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5569_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5569_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5569_Task13" name="Customer &amp; employee messaging">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer &amp; employee messaging: opening status and service levels pushed to store channels, app/store locator and local social; employees get the transport options and the no-penalty confirmation in one communication
Responsible (R): VS-63 / Communications
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: Same morning</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5569_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5569_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5569_Task14" name="Payroll &amp; leave integrity">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Payroll &amp; leave integrity: attendance coding per the directive (transport-disruption code — no absence-hit, no unverified absent); partial-day attendance tracked; the coding rides W10-class payroll rails
Responsible (R): Payroll (VS-19.2)
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Per cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5569_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5569_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5569_Task15" name="After-action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: After-action: attendance-vs-forecast reconciliation, shuttle-surge utilization, corridor vulnerability register update (chronic corridors pre-plan consolidated pickups), and the multi-day playbook refresh
Responsible (R): Transport Lead / HR
Accountable (A): Head of HR Shared Services
Duration: Post-event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5569_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5569_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5569_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5569_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5569_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-654 (ensure controlled execution — Shuttle Service, Route &amp; Daily Commute Operations (PA-141.2).) | - operational: attendance coding under a declared commute disruption uses the no-penalty category verified against the event record; surge transport runs on W4250 manifests with W4253-gated allowances; any trading-day closure rides the E-02 custody and is documented either way
Owner: Transport Lead / Fleet Planning (VS-06) (continuity protocol); Site Managers (attendance execution)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5569_Assoc18" sourceRef="W5569_Annotation17" targetRef="W5569_Start8" associationDirection="None" />
